<title>BELGIUM: Belgian 1997/8 beet crop gets off to slow start.</title>
<headline>Belgian 1997/8 beet crop gets off to slow start.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian sugar beet plantings have got off to a slow start for the 1997/98 season, with just one-third of one percent of the planned 100,989 hectare area sown so far, the sugar beet association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said 328 ha of the crop had been sown as of March 17.</p>
<p>In 1996 the country harvested 103,849 ha of beet sugar.</p>
</text>
